A||||13||artherd||Quick good mod. (88s)||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||08-12-2001||11:59 PM||||My formula has good engine/tranny/dogbone mounts (new ones infact) but it still would "lurch" a bit.<P>So I cut a piece of 1/4" steel and bolted and expoxied (you could weld too...) it on top of the driver's side rearmost toe-link on the engine cradle.<P>This put it between the cradle and the little "bump stop" and took up all the slack.<P>Bingo, car is as tight as can be, and no increase in vibration, etc at all!<P>Took about 5min, and greatly increased the drivability of the car in all situations!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||08-13-2001||12:03 AM||||got any pics to show what you mean? sounds pretty interesting<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||08-13-2001||12:35 AM||||I think he's talking about the little "foot" that sticks out from drivers side of the tranny, about 1" above cradle. Once this 1" is absorbed, the "foot" contacts the cradle, reducing "rocking". He just got rid of the allowable "slack." Sounds interesting, but GM put the space there for a reason, so I would be hesitant to try it out. I've guinea pigged enough stuff and lost, I don't do that kinda' thing anymore($$$).||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||08-13-2001||07:49 AM||||That's what I was talking about allright, though in my car there was exactly .268" of clearance (new mounts and all?)<P>I think GM only kept it because they're used to building soft cars, not sports cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The thing to do is take up all of the slack by just adding a piece of metal or such (smooth so it doesn't tear the 'foot')<P>It's really great, I've been driven mad by how sloppy fiero drivetrains can be even with new parts.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Alex4mula||08-13-2001||09:00 AM||||My Formula has a lot of slack & movement even with new mounts. I would be very interested in this but still don't understand what area exactly you are talking about. Any picture of the area? TIA.||||reg||1
Z||000005||KissMySSFiero||08-13-2001||09:27 AM||||ok i see what ya mean.  it was late and i had been working on my car for about 10 hours.  ill hit that one up when i get to the rears suspension.  exellent idea.  thanks||||reg||1
